herdr — https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Portions of Recoder's conductor attention detection are derived from herdr:

  - backend/src/domains/conductor/attention/attention-manifests.ts
  - backend/src/domains/conductor/attention/attention-manifests-core.ts
  - backend/src/domains/conductor/attention/attention-manifests-agents.ts
        The declarative per-agent terminal-state detection engine
        (region/matcher/priority model) and the per-agent rule corpus are
        ported from herdr's detection manifests (src/detect/manifest.rs and
        src/detect/manifests/*.toml), re-expressed in Recoder's AttentionState
        vocabulary. herdr's Idle-fallback default is deliberately dropped in
        favour of Recoder's truthful "unknown when no signal" invariant.

  - backend/src/domains/conductor/attention/attention-debounce.ts
        The working->idle confirmation debounce is a clean-room re-expression
        of herdr's PendingIdleConfirmation (src/pane/agent_detection.rs).

  - backend/src/domains/conductor/attention/attention-priority.ts
        The attention priority ordering is inspired by herdr's status ranking.

  - backend/src/domains/conductor/adapters/tmux-substrate.adapter.ts
        The git-worktree branch-safety and gated-cleanup design is inspired by
        herdr's src/worktree.rs (clean-room, design only).

Changes: rule sets adapted to Recoder's runtime set and AttentionState
vocabulary; OSC-progress rules omitted (no Recoder capture surface); truthful
unknown-default substituted for herdr's Idle fallback. See
docs/COMPETITIVE-HERDR.md for the full analysis and attribution rationale.
