Copyright (c) 2026 T3 Tools Inc. Licensed under the MIT License.

t3code @ commit d720210996a514368ba99f4860063110033d93fa (2026-10-07, v0.0.45)
is vendored under third_party/t3code via `git subtree add --squash`, per
docs/T3CODE-FORK.md. Its LICENSE is retained verbatim at
third_party/t3code/LICENSE. `apps/desktop` (t3's own Electron shell) and
`apps/marketing` (its Astro site) were removed from the vendored tree on
import — Recoder ships one desktop shell only (the Wave fork) and keeps
recoder.xyz as its own marketing site; only patterns from those two apps are
mined, not their code.

`third_party/t3code/apps/server` (the `recoder` CLI, née `t3`) and its
`apps/web` are now live build/consumption targets (docs/T3CODE-FORK.md
section 9/12): `packages/t3-bridge` (section 3) is the only place allowed to
import `@t3tools/*` internals into Recoder's backend runtime (the terminal
and governance seams, section 4); `packages/t3-session-bridge` is the
analogous seam on the Wave desktop side, wrapping `@t3tools/contracts`'
`WsRpcGroup` wire schema for the `recoder-session` Wave block
(apps/desktop/app/frontend/app/view/recoder-session). Nothing else imports
`@t3tools/*` directly. Internal package names, Effect service names, and wire
field names inside third_party/t3code stay upstream-shaped (same policy as
Wave's `wsh`/`WAVETERM_*` and herdr/Loom's pre-rebrand internals) so
`git subtree pull` stays a clean sync, not a re-rename pass. Only user-facing
strings are rebranded, via the scripted, re-appliable patch at
scripts/rebrand-t3code.sh (never hand-edited into the vendored tree
permanently).

MIT is compatible with the Apache-2.0 code already vendored here (Wave,
herdr/Loom, cloudflared).
